From a63125968fbe22cf848d4e3990e9fb97bf8802b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikodem Okrajni <nikodem.okrajni@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:10:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 129/194] power: supply: qcom_smbx: Fix battery overvoltage
 status

smbx_ov_status() tests the register offset instead of the value it
just read, so the result depends only on the offset and is always 0
for both generations: BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_2 (0x07) & BIT(5) on SMB2
and BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_7 (0x0d) & BIT(1) on SMB5. Battery
overvoltage is never reported.

Testing the value alone is not enough on SMB5. There the BAT_OV bit is
BIT(1) of BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_2, as in downstream smb5-reg.h
(CHARGER_ERROR_STATUS_BAT_OV_BIT) and smb5-lib.c. BIT(1) of
BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_7 is BAT_TEMP_STATUS_TOO_HOT_AFP_BIT, so reading
STATUS_7 would report a temperature fault as overvoltage.

Test the value read, and read STATUS_2 on SMB5.

Fixes: d3f6a47f4af3 ("FROMLIST v1 power: supply: qcom_smbx: add smb5 support")
Link: https://github.com/sm7150-mainline/linux/issues/63
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 973ae476b..bbd07a176 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -365,7 +365,7 @@ static int smbx_ov_status(struct smb_chip *chip)
 		mask = SMB2_CHARGER_ERROR_STATUS_BAT_OV_BIT;
 		break;
 	case SMB5:
-		reg = BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_7;
+		reg = BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_2;
 		mask = SMB5_CHARGER_ERROR_STATUS_BAT_OV_BIT;
 		break;
 	}
